<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Look-ahead Modulation Efficiency</h3>

<figure id="A4.F15" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A4.F15.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05825v1/eval_benchmark_aime-2024_1.5B_20250810_predictive_compute_cost.svg" id="A4.F15.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/425;" width="548" height="425"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>AIME 2024 (Qwen2.5-1.5B)</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A4.F15.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05825v1/eval_benchmark_aime-2024_7B_20250912_predictive_compute_cost.svg" id="A4.F15.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/425;" width="548" height="425"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span>AIME 2024 (Qwen2.5-7B)</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 15: </span>AIME-24 results with Qwen-2.5-1.5b-Instruct and Qwen-2.5-7b-Instruct for Entropic Particle Filtering and Look-Ahead Modulation.
We run ePF w/ LaM until it reaches performance within 5% of the ePF with <math id="A4.F15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=32</annotation></semantics></math>.
We can see that ePF w/ LaM and 8 particles reaches a performance comparable to ePF with 32 particles using a Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct model.
And ePF w/ LaM and 16 particles is competitive with ePF with 32 particles using a Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct model.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A4.F16" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A4.F16.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05825v1/x1.svg" id="A4.F16.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/418;" width="548" height="418"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>AIME 2024 (Qwen3-0.6B)</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A4.F16.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05825v1/x2.svg" id="A4.F16.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/418;" width="548" height="418"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span>AIME 2025 (Qwen3-1.7B)</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 16: </span>AIME-24 and AIME-25 results with Qwen3-0.6B and Qwen3-1.7B w/o thinking mode for ePF and ePF w/ LaM.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A4.F17" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A4.F17.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05825v1/x3.svg" id="A4.F17.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/439;" width="548" height="439"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>Task Reward by Budget.</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A4.F17.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05825v1/aime_2025_1.7b_running_median_predictive.svg" id="A4.F17.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/431;" width="548" height="431"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span>Running Task Reward over Budgets.</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 17: </span>Task reward comparison on AIME-2025 using Qwen3-1.7B. Our Entropic Particle Filtering (<span id="A4.F17.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ePF</span>) and its Look-ahead variant (<span id="A4.F17.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ePF</span> w/ <span id="A4.F17.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">LaM</span>) significantly improve performance over standard Particle Filtering (PF) across all particle budgets. This demonstrates that mitigating premature exploitation leads to significant performance gains.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.4 </span>PF and ePF Max Performance</h3>

<figure id="A4.F18" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A4.F18.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05825v1/eval_benchmark_aime-2024_1.5B_20250912_long_seq.svg" id="A4.F18.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/425;" width="548" height="425"></object>
