</section>
<section id="A4.SS8" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.8 </span>Temperature Schedule Ablation</h3>

<div id="A4.SS8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While particle filtering ideally explores the search space by resampling from a diverse set of particles, it often suffers from premature collapse. This issue arises when the search process oversamples a few promising particles too early, often due to misspecified rewards or overconfidence. This effectively turns the algorithm into a greedy search, which is particularly detrimental for complex problems as it stifles thorough exploration. To counteract this, we introduce an annealing strategy that modulates the temperature of the resampling distribution to preserve particle diversity and mitigate early exploitation.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS8.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS8.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To control this process, we introduce a dynamically adjusted temperature, <math id="A4.SS8.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\beta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\beta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, which follows an annealing schedules at each time step <math id="A4.SS8.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> (Fig. <a href="#A4.F21" title="Figure 21 ‣ D.8 Temperature Schedule Ablation ‣ Appendix D Additional Experiments ‣ Mitigating Premature Exploitation in Particle-based Monte Carlo for Inference-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>). Two of these schedules adaptively respond to particle diversity, which we quantify using the normalized entropy,</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS8.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A4.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{n}(t)=-\frac{\sum^{N}_{i=1}w^{i}_{t}\log w^{i}_{t}}{\log N}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{n}(t)=-\frac{\sum^{N}_{i=1}w^{i}_{t}\log w^{i}_{t}}{\log N},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS8.p3.1" class="ltx_p">and the effective sample size,</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS8.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A4.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ESS(t)=\dfrac{1}{\sum^{N}_{j=1}(w^{j}_{t})^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ESS(t)=\dfrac{1}{\sum^{N}_{j=1}(w^{j}_{t})^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS8.p4.1" class="ltx_p">ESS and Entropy are closely related <span id="footnote2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">2</span>
              
              
              
            One way to define <math id="footnote2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ESS(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ESS(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="footnote2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp{(H(t))}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp{(H(t))}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Martino &amp; Elvira (2025)</a></cite>.</span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS8.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS8.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The proposed schedules are (Figure <a href="#A4.F21" title="Figure 21 ‣ D.8 Temperature Schedule Ablation ‣ Appendix D Additional Experiments ‣ Mitigating Premature Exploitation in Particle-based Monte Carlo for Inference-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>):</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS8.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Linear</em>: a simple decay schedule, <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}^{-1}=k-t/T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}^{-1}=k-t/T</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">ESS-based</em>: a temperature schedule defined as <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}^{-1}=(N/ESS(t))\cdot(1-t/T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}^{-1}=(N/ESS(t))\cdot(1-t/T)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Entropy-based</em>: a convex combination given by <math id="A4.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}=H_{n}(t)+(1-H_{n}(t))\cdot t/T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}=H_{n}(t)+(1-H_{n}(t))\cdot t/T</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS8.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS8.p7.1" class="ltx_p">At each step, the resulting inverse temperature <math id="A4.SS8.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> modulates the particle rewards <math id="A4.SS8.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{i}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{i}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> to produce the resampling weights via a softmax function (Fig. <a href="#S3.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 3.2 Entropic Particle Filtering (ePF) ‣ 3 Method ‣ Mitigating Premature Exploitation in Particle-based Monte Carlo for Inference-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>):</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS8.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A4.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{i}_{t}=\frac{\exp(r^{i}_{t}\cdot\beta_{t})}{\sum^{N}_{j=1}\exp(r^{j}_{t}\cdot\beta_{t})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{i}_{t}=\frac{\exp(r^{i}_{t}\cdot\beta_{t})}{\sum^{N}_{j=1}\exp(r^{j}_{t}\cdot\beta_{t})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F21" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05825v1/softmax_schedules.svg" id="A4.F21.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:247/247;" width="247" height="247"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 21: </span>Different Schedules for the resampling distribution temperature annealing increasing the number of sampling steps.
Here we set <math id="A4.F21.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=2</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.F21.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{n}=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{n}=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.F21.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=16</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A4.F21.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ess(t)=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ess(t)=8</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A4.F22" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A4.F22.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05825v1/eval_ablation_schedule_aime-2024_7B_20250911.svg" id="A4.F22.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/425;" width="548" height="425"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>AIME 2024 (Qwen2.5-7B)</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A4.F22.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05825v1/eval_ablation_schedule_aime-2024_1.7B_20250911.svg" id="A4.F22.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/419;" width="548" height="419"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span>AIME 2024 (Qwen3-1.7B)</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A4.F22.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05825v1/eval_ablation_schedule_aime-2025_7B_20250911.svg" id="A4.F22.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/419;" width="548" height="419"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(c) </span>AIME 2025 (Qwen2.5-7B)</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A4.F22.sf4" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05825v1/eval_ablation_schedule_aime-2025_1.7B_20250911.svg" id="A4.F22.sf4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/425;" width="548" height="425"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(d) </span>AIME 2025 (Qwen3-1.7B)</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 22: </span>Temperature Schedule ablation for AIME-24 and AIME-25 using Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct and Qwen3-1.7B. Among models and datasets, ESS-based temperature annealing is the most consistent.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A4.SS8.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS8.p9.1" class="ltx_p">See Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ Appendix F Algorithms ‣ Mitigating Premature Exploitation in Particle-based Monte Carlo for Inference-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> for implementation details and Figure <a href="#A4.F22" title="Figure 22 ‣ D.8 Temperature Schedule Ablation ‣ Appendix D Additional Experiments ‣ Mitigating Premature Exploitation in Particle-based Monte Carlo for Inference-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a> for a temperature schedule ablation over AIME-2024 and AIME-2025.
If not otherwise specified, we use the <em id="A4.SS8.p9.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">ESS-based</em> schedule for the core experiments.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS8.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS8.p10.1" class="ltx_p">The ESS-based schedule is designed to react aggressively to particle collapse. When the ESS is low (indicating low diversity), the temperature sharply increases to encourage exploration. The <math id="A4.SS8.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-t/T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-t/T)</annotation></semantics></math> term ensures this exploratory pressure is strongest in the early stages and gradually anneals or cools over time, allowing the search to shift from exploration to exploitation as it progresses (Fig. <a href="#A4.F21" title="Figure 21 ‣ D.8 Temperature Schedule Ablation ‣ Appendix D Additional Experiments ‣ Mitigating Premature Exploitation in Particle-based Monte Carlo for Inference-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS9" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.9 </span>Effective Sample Size Ablation</h3>

<figure id="A4.F23" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05825v1/ess_aime24_epf_lam_2budget.svg" id="A4.F23.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:165/160;" width="165" height="160"></object></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05825v1/ess_epf_lam_2budget.svg" id="A4.F23.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:165/160;" width="165" height="160"></object></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05825v1/ess_aime24_epf_lam_4budget.svg" id="A4.F23.g3" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:165/163;" width="165" height="163"></object></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05825v1/ess_epf_lam_4budget.svg" id="A4.F23.g4" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:165/163;" width="165" height="163"></object></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05825v1/ess_aime24_epf_lam_8budget.svg" id="A4.F23.g5" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:165/160;" width="165" height="160"></object></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05825v1/ess_epf_lam_8budget.svg" id="A4.F23.g6" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:165/160;" width="165" height="160"></object></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05825v1/ess_aime24_epf_lam_16budget.svg" id="A4.F23.g7" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:165/165;" width="165" height="165"></object></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05825v1/ess_epf_lam_16budget.svg" id="A4.F23.g8" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:165/160;" width="165" height="160"></object></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05825v1/ess_aime24_epf_lam_32budget.svg" id="A4.F23.g9" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:165/165;" width="165" height="165"></object></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05825v1/ess_epf_lam_32budget.svg" id="A4.F23.g10" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:165/165;" width="165" height="165"></object></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 23: </span>Running Effective Sample Size (post-resampling) for AIME 2024 and AIME 2025 using Qwen3-1.7B over increasing budgets <math id="A4.F23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\in\{2,4,8,16,32\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\in\{2,4,8,16,32\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS10" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.10 </span>Coverage and Diversity</h3>

<figure id="A4.F24" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A4.F24.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05825v1/x4.svg" id="A4.F24.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:548/534;" width="548" height="534"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>AIME 2024 (Qwen3-1.7B)</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A4.F24.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05825v1/x5.svg" id="A4.F24.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:548/534;" width="548" height="534"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span>AIME 2025 (Qwen3-1.7B)</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A4.F24.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05825v1/diversity_k_aime_2024_1.7b_comparison.svg" id="A4.F24.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:548/603;" width="548" height="603"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(c) </span>AIME 2024 (Qwen3-1.7B)</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A4.F24.sf4" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05825v1/diversity_k_aime_2025_1.7b_comparison.svg" id="A4.F24.sf4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:548/592;" width="548" height="592"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(d) </span>AIME 2025 (Qwen3-1.7B)</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 24: </span>Diversity of Correct Solutions for pass@1 and pass@B generating up to 12k tokens/sequence. pass@B is defined as the expected pass@1 aggregated over budgets. The goal of mitigating early exploitation in PF is to maintain a distribution over hypotheses and do not over-optimize early on in the sampling process. Given that ePF is exploring more, we expect the algorithm to find more diverse solutions.</figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="A4.SS10.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Syntactic Diversity</h4>

<div id="A4.SS10.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS10.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For syntactic diversity, we consider the Jaccard coefficient, which measures the similarity between two sets. Given two responses, <math id="A4.SS10.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{a}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS10.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{b}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A4.SS10.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{a}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS10.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{b}</annotation></semantics></math> be their respective sets of unique tokens. The Jaccard coefficient is defined as <math id="A4.SS10.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(T_{a},T_{b})=\frac{|T_{a}\cap T_{b}|}{|T_{a}\cup T_{b}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(T_{a},T_{b})=\frac{|T_{a}\cap T_{b}|}{|T_{a}\cup T_{b}|}</annotation></semantics></math>. A lower Jaccard coefficient indicates less overlap in vocabulary and thus greater syntactic diversity. The Jaccard distance, defined as <math id="A4.SS10.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-J(T_{a},T_{b})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-J(T_{a},T_{b})</annotation></semantics></math>, provides a complementary view, where a higher value signifies greater dissimilarity. By averaging the pairwise Jaccard distance across all response pairs, we can obtain an overall measure of syntactic diversity for the entire set of responses; see Figure <a href="#A4.F25" title="Figure 25 ‣ Syntactic Diversity ‣ D.10 Coverage and Diversity ‣ Appendix D Additional Experiments ‣ Mitigating Premature Exploitation in Particle-based Monte Carlo for Inference-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F25" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A4.F25.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05825v1/diversity_syntax_aime_2025_1.7b_comparison.svg" id="A4.F25.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:548/1148;" width="548" height="1148"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>AIME 2025 (Qwen3-1.7B)</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A4.F25.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05825v1/diversity_semantic_aime_2025_1.7b_comparison.svg" id="A4.F25.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:548/652;" width="548" height="652"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span>AIME 2025 (Qwen3-1.7B)</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 25: </span>Syntactic (left) and Semantic (right) Dissimilarity between selected trajectories using Particle Filtering and Entropic Particle Filtering. Entropic Particle Filtering tends to generate responses that are more syntactically and semantically diverse.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A4.F26" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05825v1/diversity_semantic_l2_aime_2025_1.7b_comparison.svg" id="A4.F26.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/182;" width="548" height="182"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 26: </span>Semantic diversity measured using average pairwise <math id="A4.F26.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> distance across embeddings from three models. We compare Particle Filtering and Entropic Particle Filtering across all AIME 2025 questions using responses generated by the Qwen3-1.7B model. The analysis is based on the first <math id="A4.F26.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> tokens of each response. Entropic Particle Filtering tends to generate responses that are more semantically diverse according to the <math id="A4.F26.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> distance metric.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS10.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Semantic Diversity</h4>

<div id="A4.SS10.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS10.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To quantify the semantic diversity among a set of <math id="A4.SS10.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=6</annotation></semantics></math> generated responses, <math id="A4.SS10.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{r_{1},r_{2},\dots,r_{N}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{r_{1},r_{2},\dots,r_{N}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we introduce a Semantic Entropy score. First, each response <math id="A4.SS10.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is encoded into a normalized embedding vector <math id="A4.SS10.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{e}_{i}=\text{model}(r_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>model</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{e}_{i}=\text{model}(r_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A4.SS10.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{e}_{i}\|_{2}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{e}_{i}\|_{2}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, using one of three sentence-embedding models: <span id="A4.SS10.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">all-mpnet-base-v2</span>, <span id="A4.SS10.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">BAAI/bge-large-en-v1.5</span>, or <span id="A4.SS10.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">BAAI/bge-m3</span>, which map text into a semantic vector space suitable for similarity comparisons. A pairwise cosine similarity matrix, <math id="A4.SS10.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐒</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}</annotation></semantics></math>, is then computed, where <math id="A4.SS10.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{ij}=\mathbf{e}_{i}\cdot\mathbf{e}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{ij}=\mathbf{e}_{i}\cdot\mathbf{e}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. To ensure a response is not compared with itself, the diagonal elements of <math id="A4.SS10.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐒</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}</annotation></semantics></math> are set to negative infinity, i.e., <math id="A4.SS10.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{ii}=-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{ii}=-\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. Next, a row-wise softmax function with a temperature parameter <math id="A4.SS10.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> is applied to this matrix to obtain a probability distribution for each response over its neighbors: <math id="A4.SS10.SSS0.Px2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(j|i)=\frac{\exp(S_{ij}/\tau)}{\sum_{k\neq i}\exp(S_{ik}/\tau)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(j|i)=\frac{\exp(S_{ij}/\tau)}{\sum_{k\neq i}\exp(S_{ik}/\tau)}</annotation></semantics></math>. These individual distributions are then aggregated into a single mean probability distribution, <math id="A4.SS10.SSS0.Px2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mathbf{p}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐩</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mathbf{p}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A4.SS10.SSS0.Px2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{p}_{j}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}p(j|i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{p}_{j}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}p(j|i)</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, the Sem-Ent score is calculated as the Shannon entropy of this aggregated distribution, <math id="A4.SS10.SSS0.Px2.p1.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H(\bar{\mathbf{p}})=-\sum_{j=1}^{N}\bar{p}_{j}\log(\bar{p}_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐩</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\bar{\mathbf{p}})=-\sum_{j=1}^{N}\bar{p}_{j}\log(\bar{p}_{j})</annotation></semantics></math>, normalized by the maximum possible entropy for <math id="A4.SS10.SSS0.Px2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N-1</annotation></semantics></math> choices, which is <math id="A4.SS10.SSS0.Px2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(N-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(N-1)</annotation></semantics></math>. The final score is clamped to the range <math id="A4.SS10.SSS0.Px2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. As a complementary measure, we also compute the average pairwise <math id="A4.SS10.SSS0.Px2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> distance between response embeddings, again using the same three models. For each set of <math id="A4.SS10.SSS0.Px2.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=6</annotation></semantics></math> responses, we calculate the <math id="A4.SS10.SSS0.Px2.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> norm between every pair of embeddings and average across all <math id="A4.SS10.SSS0.Px2.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{N}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{N}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> pairs and all questions. A higher value indicates greater semantic diversity; see Figures <a href="#A4.F25" title="Figure 25 ‣ Syntactic Diversity ‣ D.10 Coverage and Diversity ‣ Appendix D Additional Experiments ‣ Mitigating Premature Exploitation in Particle-based Monte Carlo for Inference-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a> and <a href="#A4.F26" title="Figure 26 ‣ Syntactic Diversity ‣ D.10 Coverage and Diversity ‣ Appendix D Additional Experiments ‣ Mitigating Premature Exploitation in Particle-based Monte Carlo for Inference-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Entropic Particle Filtering Pipeline</h2>

<figure id="A5.F27" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A5.F27.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05825v1/ea_lam_iclr.svg" id="A5.F27.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/90;" width="548" height="90"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>Entropic Annealing (EA) and Look-ahead Modulation (LaM).</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A5.F27.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05825v1/full_image_pipeline.svg" id="A5.F27.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/249;" width="548" height="249"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span>Entropic Particle Filtering (ePF).</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 27: </span>Entropic Particle Filtering Pipeline (ePF; Fig. <a href="#A5.F27.sf2" title="In Figure 27 ‣ Appendix E Entropic Particle Filtering Pipeline ‣ Mitigating Premature Exploitation in Particle-based Monte Carlo for Inference-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27(b)</span></a>). Our method iteratively refines a set of <math id="A5.F27.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> particles (states <math id="A5.F27.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>) for a given prompt <math id="A5.F27.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{c}</annotation></semantics></math>. In each step <math id="A5.F27.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, particles are propagated by sampling a language model, <math id="A5.F27.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{z}_{t}|\mathbf{z}_{t-1},\mathbf{c})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{z}_{t}|\mathbf{z}_{t-1},\mathbf{c})</annotation></semantics></math>, and then weighted by a reward model, <math id="A5.F27.m16" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="r(\mathbf{z}_{1:t},\mathbf{c})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(\mathbf{z}_{1:t},\mathbf{c})</annotation></semantics></math>. A resampling step, guided by these weights, approximates the posterior <math id="A5.F27.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{z}_{t}|\mathbf{o}_{t},\mathbf{c})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐨</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{z}_{t}|\mathbf{o}_{t},\mathbf{c})</annotation></semantics></math> to concentrate on promising candidates. After convergence, a final solution <math id="A5.F27.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math> is decoded via <math id="A5.F27.m19" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p(\mathbf{x}|\mathbf{z}_{1:T},\mathbf{c})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{x}|\mathbf{z}_{1:T},\mathbf{c})</annotation></semantics></math>. To prevent premature convergence, we introduce two complementary mechanisms: <em id="A5.F27.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Entropic Annealing</em> (EA; Fig. <a href="#A5.F27.sf1" title="In Figure 27 ‣ Appendix E Entropic Particle Filtering Pipeline ‣ Mitigating Premature Exploitation in Particle-based Monte Carlo for Inference-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27(a)</span></a> left), which preserves diversity by dynamically annealing the resampling distribution <math id="A5.F27.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> based on entropy, and <em id="A5.F27.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Look-ahead Modulation</em> (LaM; Fig. <a href="#A5.F27.sf1" title="In Figure 27 ‣ Appendix E Entropic Particle Filtering Pipeline ‣ Mitigating Premature Exploitation in Particle-based Monte Carlo for Inference-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27(a)</span></a> right), which steers the search toward more promising future states. This dual strategy guides the algorithm toward regions of both high reward and high diversity, effectively mitigating convergence to suboptimal local solutions.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Algorithms</h2>

<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Particle Filtering (PF)</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
            
            
          
</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
            
            
          <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{c}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l2.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Task Input; Particle Budget; Steps
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
            
            
          <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{z}_{t}|\mathbf{z}_{t-1},\mathbf{c})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{z}_{t}|\mathbf{z}_{t-1},\mathbf{c})</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l3.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Sampling/Dynamics Model
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
            
            
          <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{o}_{t}|\mathbf{z}_{t},\mathbf{c})=\delta(s-g(\mathbf{z}_{t},\mathbf{c}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐨</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{o}_{t}|\mathbf{z}_{t},\mathbf{c})=\delta(s-g(\mathbf{z}_{t},\mathbf{c}))</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l4.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Reward/Observation Model
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
            
            
          
</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
            
            
          <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{1}\sim p(\mathbf{z}_{1}|\mathbf{c})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{1}\sim p(\mathbf{z}_{1}|\mathbf{c})</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l6.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Sample initial step
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
            
            
          <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{1}\leftarrow 1/N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{1}\leftarrow 1/N</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l7.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Initialize weights
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
            
            
          <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}=\{(\mathbf{z}^{i}_{1},w^{i}_{1})\}^{N}_{i=1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}=\{(\mathbf{z}^{i}_{1},w^{i}_{1})\}^{N}_{i=1}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l8.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Initialize Particles
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> step <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=2</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> particle <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span> <span id="alg1.l10.4" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> State Estimation step <math id="alg1.l10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}^{i}_{t}\sim p(\mathbf{z}_{t}|\mathbf{z}_{t-1},\mathbf{c})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}^{i}_{t}\sim p(\mathbf{z}_{t}|\mathbf{z}_{t-1},\mathbf{c})</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l11.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Propagation
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="s^{i}_{t}\leftarrow g(\mathbf{z}^{i}_{t:T},\mathbf{c})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{i}_{t}\leftarrow g(\mathbf{z}^{i}_{t:T},\mathbf{c})</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l12.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Scoring
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{i}_{t}\leftarrow\log s^{i}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{i}_{t}\leftarrow\log s^{i}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">14:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">15:</span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="w^{i}_{t}\leftarrow\exp(r^{i}_{t})/\sum^{N}_{j=1}\exp(r^{j}_{t}),\quad i=1,...,N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">/</mo><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{i}_{t}\leftarrow\exp(r^{i}_{t})/\sum^{N}_{j=1}\exp(r^{j}_{t}),\quad i=1,...,N</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l15.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Compute Resampling Distribution
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">16:</span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{k_{i}\}^{N}_{i=1}\sim\texttt{Multinomial}\left[w_{t}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Multinomial</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{k_{i}\}^{N}_{i=1}\sim\texttt{Multinomial}\left[w_{t}\right]</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="alg1.l16.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Sample <math id="alg1.l16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> indexes with Replacement
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">17:</span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{t}\leftarrow\mathbf{z}_{t}\left[k_{1:N}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{t}\leftarrow\mathbf{z}_{t}\left[k_{1:N}\right]</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l17.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Sample Selection
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">18:</span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}\leftarrow\mathcal{P}\cup\{(\mathbf{z}_{t},w_{t})\}^{N}_{i=1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>∪</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}\leftarrow\mathcal{P}\cup\{(\mathbf{z}_{t},w_{t})\}^{N}_{i=1}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l18.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Update Particles
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">19:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l19.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l19.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">20:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l20.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg1.l20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{x}\sim p(\mathbf{x}|\mathbf{z}_{1:T},\mathbf{c})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}\sim p(\mathbf{x}|\mathbf{z}_{1:T},\mathbf{c})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
